dh_virtualenv installs from PyPI during the build, so this package cannot be
built in sbuild's default offline chroot. build/build-package.sh passes
--enable-network when this marker is present.

This is a deliberate, narrow exception to Debian's "builds must be offline"
rule, and it is per-package rather than global so that tlosint-meta and
tlosint-config keep the stronger guarantee.

What keeps it honest: requirements.txt is fully hash-pinned and carries a
--require-hashes directive, so the build can only ever install the exact
artifacts we locked. Network access cannot change what lands in the package,
only whether the build succeeds at all.

The alternative -- vendoring wheels into the source package -- was rejected:
it would mean committing ~42 MB of binaries to main, which handoff section 8
forbids, and the wheels would have to be downloaded with the chroot's exact
interpreter and platform tags rather than the host's.
